Licence layers of this package
1. Code (scripts/): MIT, as above. Exception: the few lines copied from the official S&I 2025 baseline that are listed in
   docs/THIRD_PARTY_CODE.md remain with their owner and are not covered by the MIT licence.
2. Documentation written by the authors (README.md, docs/, the text of configs/ and environment/): CC BY 4.0
   (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), except the corpus-derived statistics they quote (layer 3) and the third-party
   lines in environment/patches/ (layer 4).
3. results/ and all corpus-derived statistics wherever they appear (including numbers quoted in README.md, docs/ and configs/):
   NO open licence is granted. Subject to the Speak & Improve Corpus 2025 licence; released subject to CUP&A approval
   (requested 2026-11-11). See docs/DATA_LICENSE_NOTE.md.
4. environment/patches/: diffs of the official S&I 2025 baseline (no licence stated; zero-context diffs with only the changed lines)
   and build records of NIST SCTK 2.4.9 (public domain) / tranfilt 1.14. The third-party lines remain with their owners; only our
   own added lines are CC BY 4.0 (environment/patches/README.md).
GRECO-related scripts (g_greco_*.py, e_after_q.sh) import the separately obtained GPL-3.0 GRECO code at run time; running them
together with GRECO is subject to the GPL-3.0.

Not included, each under its own licence: GRECO code (GPL-3.0); the Speak & Improve Corpus 2025 and everything derived from it
at the level of utterances or edits (labels, features, model outputs, trained models); the official S&I baseline code and models;
the pretrained models.
